      "id": 1,
      "text": "Colona was formed in 1997 when the former City of Green Rock and the Village of Colona merged by popular vote, the first such merger in Illinois.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colona%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city sits in a valley beside the Rock River, surrounded by higher ground that gives it a distinctive topography.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colona%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Here the Green River and the historic Hennepin Canal empty into the Rock River, a notable confluence in the region.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colona%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Colona is part of the Quad Cities metropolitan area, linking it culturally and economically to the larger regional community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Colona%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Quad Cities MetroLINK Route 30 provides bus service that connects Colona directly to destinations across the Quad Cities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
